ser methods =======================--\nMethod: Birth \nParameters:\nme - the script of this object, should be: script \"slideShow control parent script\"\ntheQtSpriteNum - the sprite number of the QuickTime movie\ntheQueListField - the name or number of the que list Field\nthePreLoadList - the nmae or number of the preLoad list field\ntheUnLoadList - the name or number of the unload list field\ntheQueFramesListField - the name or number of the list of que frames field\nReturn: this instance\nDoes: initiate the object\n\n\nMethod: edKill\nParameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: remove the object from the actorList and retunr void. use it as follow:\ngMyObj = kill( gMyObj )\n\nMethod: onMouseUp\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: Move the QT to the end of it in a case of mouse click. you should call this method from a movie mouseUp method.\n\nMethod: onIdle\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: calls the preloader onidle method\nyou should call this method from an ON IDLE event in your movie.\n\nMethod: edGetName\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: return #slideShowControl\nDoes: return the name of this object.\n\n--=========================== End of user methods =======================--\n\n--====================== start of object internal methods ====================--\n\nMethod: stepFrame\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: decide wether we reached a new que. If so advance to the next que, otherwise, loop the movie in the current que. If we are in record mode, it will just loop.\nThis method is called by director each time the movieHead is leaving a frame.\n\nMethod: edStepFrameForRunTime\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: check if we should go to the next Que or stay in the current que.\nThis methis is called only by stepFrame\n\nMethod: edGetLoopFrame\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: the number of frame to jump to.\nDoes: returns the number of frame to jump to according to a flag that knows if we need to loop to marker(0) or to the frame.\n\nMethod: edGoToNextQue\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes:  return the number of the next frame to go to, after updateing the curQue number to the closest one the the current QT frame. It will also update the preloader lists of preload/unload.\n\nMethod: edGetQueFrameNum\nparameters:\nwhichQue - the number of que to check\nReturn: the number of frame that this que starts with.\nDoes: retreive the number of the first frame that the given que starts in.\n\nMethod: edUpdateLoopMode\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: set the property fLoopOneFrame to True if current frame name have the string \",loopOneFrame\" at the end of it. otherwise it will set it to False.\n\nMethod: edCleanOldInstance\nparameters:\nme - this object instance\nReturn: void\nDoes: Check if there is another instance of that object in the actorList and if so, it will remove it.\n--====================== End of object internal methods ====================--\n\n","align":0,"rect":[0,0,514,1425],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":30,"ascent":23,"style":3,"size":24,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":25,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":188,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":5,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":202,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#008000","font":"Arial"},{"start":280,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":1,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":288,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":295,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":1,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":307,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":705,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":1,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"},{"start":713,"height":16,